WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.420
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.420
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:15.344
Unit fourteen: Zero Conditional. Today you will talk about facts and rules that are always true.

4
00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:18.308
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.604
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.068
If.

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.536
If means a word that starts a condition.

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.254
If you heat ice, it melts.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.887
Your turn. Say: If.

10
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:36.363
If.

11
00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:38.257
Always true.

12
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.668
Always true means true every time.

13
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:43.923
The fact is always true.

14
00:00:44.517 --> 00:00:47.587
Your turn. Say: Always true.

15
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:51.678
Always true.

16
00:00:52.417 --> 00:00:53.696
General fact.

17
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:58.448
General fact means a truth that is usually or always correct.

18
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.166
A general fact does not change.

19
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:04.391
Your turn. Say: General fact.

20
00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.374
General fact.

21
00:01:09.117 --> 00:01:10.454
Water boils.

22
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:14.947
Water boils means a fact about water at one hundred degrees.

23
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.596
Water boils at one hundred degrees.

24
00:01:18.183 --> 00:01:20.998
Your turn. Say: Water boils.

25
00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:25.090
Water boils.

26
00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.594
Scientific fact.

27
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:31.755
Scientific fact means a truth proved by science.

28
00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:34.013
It is a scientific fact.

29
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:38.105
Your turn. Say: Scientific fact.

30
00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.513
Scientific fact.

31
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.530
Cause and effect.

32
00:01:45.517 --> 00:01:48.352
Cause and effect means a reason and its result.

33
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:51.008
Heat and melting are cause and effect.

34
00:01:51.617 --> 00:01:54.466
Your turn. Say: Cause and effect.

35
00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.580
Cause and effect.

36
00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:00.341
Present simple.

37
00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.209
Present simple means the tense for facts and habits.

38
00:02:04.817 --> 00:02:07.443
The zero conditional uses the present simple.

39
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.807
Your turn. Say: Present simple.

40
00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.958
Present simple.

41
00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:16.393
Rule.

42
00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:20.103
Rule means a statement that is always followed.

43
00:02:20.717 --> 00:02:21.811
Here is a rule.

44
00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:25.139
Your turn. Say: Rule.

45
00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.943
Rule.

46
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:33.663
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:36.830
Visal, what happens if you heat ice?

48
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:48.606
If you heat ice, it melts. This is the zero conditional. We use it for facts and rules that are always true: if + present simple, present simple.

49
00:02:49.717 --> 00:02:51.101
Can we change the order?

50
00:02:52.217 --> 00:03:01.968
Yes. It melts if you heat it. With the if-clause at the start, we put a comma: If you heat ice, it melts. In the middle, we do not need a comma.

51
00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:04.270
Can we use when?

52
00:03:05.383 --> 00:03:18.778
Yes, when has the same meaning here: When water reaches one hundred degrees, it boils. Use the zero conditional for science, habits and general rules. Do not use will.

53
00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.608
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:27.642
Grammar focus: Zero conditional: If plus present simple, present simple.

55
00:03:27.942 --> 00:03:29.059
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:31.691
If you heat ice, it melts.

57
00:03:32.583 --> 00:03:35.848
If water reaches 100 degrees, it boils.

58
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:39.307
If I am tired, I go to bed early.

59
00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:48.808
Use if + present simple, present simple for facts, rules and habits that are always true. Do not use will. When can replace if.

60
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:53.236
Be careful! Don't say: If you heat ice, it will melt.

61
00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.792
Say: If you heat ice, it melts.

62
00:03:58.092 --> 00:04:00.683
Use the present simple in a zero conditional.

63
00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:03.968
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:05.872
Always True.

65
00:04:06.172 --> 00:04:08.067
If you heat ice, it melts.

66
00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.902
Water boils when it reaches one hundred degrees.

67
00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.213
If you mix red and blue, you get purple.

68
00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.629
If I am tired, I go to bed early.

69
00:04:19.633 --> 00:04:23.177
These sentences describe a cause and effect that is always true.

70
00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:28.129
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:28.983 --> 00:04:30.716
If you heat ice, it blank.

72
00:04:31.016 --> 00:04:34.565
A, will melt. B, melts. C, melted.

73
00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.100
The answer is B: melts.

74
00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:43.400
If plants get no water, they blank.

75
00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:46.797
A, die. B, will die. C, died.

76
00:04:50.333 --> 00:04:52.019
The answer is A: die.

77
00:04:53.183 --> 00:04:55.403
Which sentence is a zero conditional?

78
00:04:55.703 --> 00:05:03.177
A, If it rains, we will stay.. B, If you mix red and blue, you get purple.. C, If I had money, I would buy it..

79
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:10.161
The answer is B: If you mix red and blue, you get purple..

80
00:05:11.317 --> 00:05:13.026
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:13.326 --> 00:05:20.555
A, If you will heat ice, it melts.. B, If you heat ice, it melts.. C, If you heated ice, it melts..

82
00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:27.388
The answer is B: If you heat ice, it melts..

83
00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:31.908
According to the reading, at what temperature does water boil?

84
00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:37.684
A, 100 degrees. B, 50 degrees. C, 0 degrees.

85
00:05:41.233 --> 00:05:43.825
The answer is A: 100 degrees.

86
00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:48.197
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:52.745
Write a zero conditional sentence about a scientific fact you know.

88
00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:03.050
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:16.872
If you mix blue and yellow, you get green. This is a scientific fact. I use the zero conditional because the result is always true, and I use the present simple in both parts.

90
00:06:17.172 --> 00:06:18.823
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:19.717 --> 00:06:26.374
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and zero conditional: if plus present simple, present simple.

92
00:06:26.674 --> 00:06:32.102
Today's value is scientific curiosity. Ask why, and then go and find out.

93
00:06:32.402 --> 00:06:35.391
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

94
00:06:35.691 --> 00:06:38.807
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

